@startuml order-to-cash
' Hand-derived from an ARIS EPC "Order to cash" following the mapping table
' in docs/business-processes.md: functions are verb-first actions, org units
' are swimlanes, events ride on arrow labels and XOR branch labels, the AND
' connector is a fork, the process interface is an action with an aris: marker. The
' footer carries the governance tags GEN006/GEN007 look for.
title Order to cash — order handling
footer owner: Sales Operations — ARIS process PROC-0042

|Sales|
start
-> Customer order received;
:Receive order;
:Validate order;
if (Order valid?) then (Order valid)
  |Credit Control|
  :Check credit limit;
  |Warehouse & Logistics|
  fork
    :Pick goods;
    :Ship goods;
  fork again
    |Finance|
    :Create invoice;
    :Send invoice;
  end fork
  |Finance|
  :Record payment;
  -> Payment received;
  stop
else (Order invalid)
  |Sales|
  :Reject order;
  ' aris: interface PROC-0051
  :Handle customer enquiry;
  -> Order rejected;
  stop
endif
@enduml
